WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:09.760
Castle was one of ABC's steadiest performers
for years, but not anymore. Following a flurry

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.790
of head-scratching headlines and behind-the-scenes
problems, the network abruptly canceled the

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:19.350
crime drama after an eight-season run. Where
did things go wrong? Well...

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.350
It's just it's complicated.

00:00:21.419 --> 00:00:23.800
Stana Katic was kicked off the show

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.509
The first sign that something was amiss on
the set of Castle came in April of 2016. ABC

00:00:28.509 --> 00:00:33.750
abruptly opted not to renew star Stana Katic's
contract for a ninth season. According &nbsp;to

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:39.140
Deadline, the decision was made due to "budgetary
reasons." To add more fuel to the fire, sources

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.960
claimed that Katic wasn't even approached
to renegotiate her contract.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.440
Even the occasional Castle viewer was shocked
by news of Katic's departure. Although the

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.980
show was named after Nathan Fillion's character,
Richard Castle, Katic's Kate Beckett had become

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:56.550
an integral part of the show's storyline.
Moving forward without Beckett made absolutely

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.640
zero sense.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.750
Sure, high-profile cast members leave shows
all the time, but considering the timing of

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:06.720
the news, plus reports that Katic didn't have
a say in her exit, the whole thing felt strange,

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.899
if not suspicious.

00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:12.840
Tamala Jones got the boot, too
Katic's departure from the show was shocking

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.639
enough, but things got crazier when another
one of Castle's top female stars, Tamala Jones,

00:01:17.639 --> 00:01:21.590
left the show as well. In all fairness, having
Jones continue to appear on Castle without

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:26.609
Katic didn't seem plausible, since her character,
Dr. Lanie Parish, was Beckett's close friend.

00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:30.569
The duo's departure seemed to suggest Castle
was preparing for a major storyline shift

00:01:30.569 --> 00:01:34.459
in Season 9. Which never would have worked
because…

00:01:34.459 --> 00:01:39.219
The show had changed too much
In its coverage of Katic's shocking departure,

00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:43.009
The Hollywood Reporter noted that the shake-up
could allow Castle to focus more on the show's

00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:47.420
weekly crime procedurals. Instead, the show
had been focusing on larger character arcs,

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:51.509
relationship troubles, and general drama.
The show had already hinted it was heading

00:01:51.509 --> 00:01:55.299
in that direction when Castle and Beckett
separated at the top of Season 8.

00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:58.920
Castle grew out of its procedural shoes a
long time ago and had since become a show

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:03.380
that many viewers were invested in because
of its characters. Returning Castle to a run-of-the-mill

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:07.749
procedural drama would have set the show back
years, when fans were expecting it to move

00:02:07.749 --> 00:02:12.080
forward. Given how the firings upset fans,
and the show's own cast, it's impossible to

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.510
imagine Castle returning to its roots without
losing viewers.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:20.519
Did Fillion and Katic hate each other?
Amid reports of Katic's exit, word got out

00:02:20.519 --> 00:02:24.720
that she and Fillion did not get along on
set, much to the heartbreak of Castle fans

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:29.599
everywhere. In fact, things allegedly got
so bad that Fillion would often make Katic

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:34.500
cry. "Stana would cry on set because Nathan
was such a bully to her," a source told Us

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.340
Weekly just days after Katic's departure hit
the wires. Added a second source: "Stana would

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:44.680
go in her dressing room and cry. A lot of
people who work on the show don't like Nathan.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.680
It's not just her. Nathan has been nasty to
Stana for a long time. Stana was a pro, just

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.689
wanted to get in there and do her job."

00:02:51.689 --> 00:02:56.280
A rep for Katic denied any on-set tension.
Fillion dodged the rumors, but his tepid "I

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:02.239
wish her well" reaction on Twitter led many
to wonder if the reports were actually true.

00:03:02.239 --> 00:03:05.510
Ratings were sluggish
When you remove all the behind-the-scenes

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:10.319
drama from Castle, ABC's decision to cancel
the show might have been a lot more rational

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:13.810
than we initially thought. The show simply
had not been pulling in the kind of ratings

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:18.790
it used to. The Season 8 premiere debuted
to just under 7 million viewers, down about

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:22.650
4 million viewers from the previous season.
Those numbers were likely an especially tough

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:26.989
pill for ABC execs to swallow, since Castle
once averaged more than 12 million viewers.

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:32.629
But the bleeding didn't stop there. In February
2016, Castle aired its midseason premiere

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:38.140
to 5.72 million viewers, a series low, according
to TV Line. By that point, the show was already

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.170
in ABC’s crosshairs.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:44.420
New showrunners were brought in
Another obvious sign that Castle's time was

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:48.640
running out. The series hired new showrunners
Alexi Hawley and Terence Paul Winter to take

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:52.959
the reins in Season 8. Hiring new people to
run a show that late in the game is never

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:58.010
a great sign. It's even worse when they make
risky changes to the storyline only to backtrack

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.650
a few episodes later.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:03.969
Such was the case with Castle and Beckett's
separation. Amid outrage from fans, Hawley

00:04:03.969 --> 00:04:08.730
and Winter were forced to go on defense, assuring
everyone that nobody was actually getting

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:12.749
divorced. But when Castle and Beckett got
back together, by taking their relationship

00:04:12.749 --> 00:04:18.090
on the DL, even that felt forced, unnecessary,
and uncreative. It seemed like Castle's new

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:21.250
showrunners were running with scissors.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:25.530
The show could not survive the negative press
Between Katic's exit, rumors of bad blood

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.560
on set, and ratings in the toilet, Castle
limped to the finish line with the kind of

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:34.330
bad press that no show could shake. Even if
Castle had returned for a ninth season, the

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:37.890
show would have spent the entire time dealing
with the fallout of getting rid of their main

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:41.860
characters. It also would have spent a good
chunk of time contending with bad press, which

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:45.760
no doubt would have ballooned the moment the
show took another dip in ratings. In other

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.230
words, by pulling the plug on Castle now,
ABC saved itself from fighting a battle it

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:54.450
was never going to win. Sad as it may sound,
it was safer to go out on a low note rather

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:57.730
than while scraping the absolute bottom of
the barrel.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:01.100
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:05.090
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know why you think Castle was really cancelled...

